### 5. Checkout → Order Creation Flow

```
1. User initiates checkout
   ↓
2. Validate cart items
   - Check reservations still valid (<15 min)
   - Verify prices haven't changed
   ↓
3. **[MONGODB TRANSACTION]**
   ├─→ Start session.startTransaction()
   ├─→
   ├─→ Create Order document
   │   - Status: PENDING_PAYMENT
   │   - Items: from cart
   │   - Calculate total with taxes
   ├─→
   ├─→ For each cart item:
   │   ├─→ Verify reserved stock
   │   └─→ Convert reservation to fulfillment
   │       - reservedStock -= qty
   │       - (no change to availableStock)
   ├─→
   ├─→ If B2B credit payment:
   │   ├─→ Check credit limit
   │   └─→ Reserve credit amount
   ├─→
   ├─→ Clear cart items
   ├─→
   ├─→ session.commitTransaction()
   └─→ [If any step fails → session.abortTransaction()]
   ↓
4. Return order ID + payment details
```

**Transaction Guarantees:**
- All-or-nothing: Order creation + Inventory update + Credit reservation
- Automatic rollback on failure
- Data consistency across collections

