### 7. Refund Flow

```
1. Admin/System initiates refund
   ↓
2. Validate refund request
   - Payment exists and is SUCCESS
   - Order is CANCELLED or RETURNED
   - Refund amount <= captured amount
   - No existing refund for this payment
   ↓
3. Create refund in Razorpay
   - POST https://api.razorpay.com/v1/payments/{paymentId}/refund
   - amount: refundAmount * 100
   ↓
4. Create Refund record in MongoDB
   - paymentId
   - razorpayRefundId
   - amount
   - status: PROCESSING
   ↓
5. Razorpay processes refund (instant/batch)
   ↓
6. Razorpay webhook: refund.created
   ↓
7. Update Refund status: COMPLETED
   ↓
8. Update Order status: REFUNDED
   ↓
9. If B2B credit payment:
   - Restore credit to customer account
   ↓
10. Queue refund confirmation email
   ↓
11. Log audit event
```

