## 🔔 Notification Workflows

### 11. Multi-Channel Notification Flow

```
Event: Order status change

1. Event triggered (e.g., order shipped)
   ↓
2. Queue notification job
   - Job data: { userId, orderId, event: 'ORDER_SHIPPED' }
   - Queue: notificationQueue (high priority)
   ↓
3. **[NOTIFICATION WORKER]**
   ├─→ Fetch user preferences
   │   - Email enabled? SMS enabled? Push enabled?
   ├─→
   ├─→ Create Notification record in MongoDB
   │   - userId, message, type, read: false
   ├─→
   ├─→ **[PARALLEL PROCESSING]**
   │   ├─→ Email notification (if enabled)
   │   │   - Queue: emailQueue
   │   │   - Template: order_shipped.html
   │   │   - Variables: trackingNumber, estimatedDelivery
   │   │
   │   ├─→ SMS notification (if enabled)
   │   │   - Queue: smsQueue
   │   │   - Template: "Your order #{orderId} shipped..."
   │   │
   │   ├─→ Push notification (if enabled)
   │   │   - Queue: pushQueue
   │   │   - Send via FCM/APNS
   │   │
   │   └─→ Real-time notification (if user online)
   │       - Socket.io emit to user's room
   │       - Event: 'notification'
   │       - Payload: notification object
   ├─→
   └─→ Log notification sent
   ↓
4. User receives notifications across channels
```

